{"base_rate":0.3394736842105263,"brier":0.19061644736842104,"bss":0.14991151672380243,"bss_hi":0.25982885378514786,"bss_lo":0.015792131098582733,"chart":{"base":[502.2,69.6],"fp":[225.7,246.3],"lead":"62,241.5 272,230.2 482,217.9 692,206.7","note":{"base":"skill 0.15 — higher than 23% of cities","fp":"low end +3pp, high end +28pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 38% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 6%; promised 100% → rained 74%"},"rel":"83.2,438.7 326.4,345.4 600.3,234.8 689.9,148"},"country":"AU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.157671052631579,"ess":343.3918522761737,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Gold Coast</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Gold Coast rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>74%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 760 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nAIR SEA RESCUE ALERT, 4.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.15, ranked 165 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(121&ndash;185) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>226</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>78%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>93%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>74%</b></td><td class='num'>163</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Gold Coast</b> <span class=\"muted\">Australia</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.15</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>121&ndash;185\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>760 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Gold Coast &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Gold Coast\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\