5263 161.70384615384614,312.0 99.3944,362.58666666666664 60.13026548672566,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"258.4315789473684\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"258.4315789473684\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"60.13026548672566,364.283185840708 99.3944,343.17333333333335 161.70384615384614,302.6666666666667 252.6534210526316,257.4736842105263 333.86347826086956,197.3623188405797 385.57123287671226,177.56164383561642 410.8272392638038,114.02453987730064\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 226 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"60.13026548672566\" cy=\"364.283185840708\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 12%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"99.3944\" cy=\"343.17333333333335\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 29%&amp;#10;It rained 22% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"161.70384615384614\" cy=\"302.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 55%&amp;#10;It rained 34% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"252.6534210526316\" cy=\"257.4736842105263\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 78%&amp;#10;It rained 51% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"333.86347826086956\" cy=\"197.3623188405797\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 93%&amp;#10;It rained 56% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"385.57123287671226\" cy=\"177.56164383561642\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 74% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 163 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.8272392638038\" cy=\"114.02453987730064\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(34%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Gold Coast the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.24) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.06).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'>-0.058</td><td class='num'>21.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'>0.036</td><td class='num'>21.4%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'>0.170</td><td class='num'>11.1%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'>0.235</td><td class='num'>11.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":-28.00029,"lon":153.43088,"n":760,"n_cities":213,"name":"Gold Coast","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.06,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.006017699115044247,"n":226,"obs":0.048672566371681415,"sig":true},{"hi":0.2,"lo":0.06,"mean":0.11693333333333335,"n":75,"obs":0.10666666666666667,"sig":false},{"hi":0.42,"lo":0.2,"mean":0.2929487179487179,"n":78,"obs":0.21794871794871795,"sig":false},{"hi":0.68,"lo":0.42,"mean":0.5498684210526316,"n":76,"obs":0.34210526315789475,"sig":true},{"hi":0.88,"lo":0.68,"mean":0.7792753623188405,"n":69,"obs":0.5072463768115942,"sig":true},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.88,"mean":0.9253424657534244,"n":73,"obs":0.5616438356164384,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9966871165644174,"n":163,"obs":0.7361963190184049,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":4.9,"provisional":false,"rank":165,"rank_hi":185.0,"rank_lo":121.0,"reliability":0.039422434827311705,"resolution":0.0730644273884577,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"gold-coast","station":"AIR SEA RESCUE ALERT","timezone":"Australia/Brisbane"}